<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Headlesses on PiHuW</title><link>https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/headless/</link><description>Recent content in Headlesses on PiHuW</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 14 Apr 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/headless/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>headless include page</title><link>https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/headless/include-example/</link><pubDate>Mon, 14 Apr 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/headless/include-example/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This is a markdown file in the &lt;code&gt;headless&lt;/code&gt; folder. It does not have a &lt;code&gt;summary&lt;/code&gt; field in the frontmatter. The &#10;&#10;&lt;a href="https://github.com/mrmxf/pihuw" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span style="color:red;"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:grey;"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:green;"&gt;H&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:grey;"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:blue;"&gt;W&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;code&gt;include&lt;/code&gt; partial will truncate the text according to the settings in the hugo config.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Markdown files may include shortcodes.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>headless include page with summary</title><link>https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/headless/include-example-summary/</link><pubDate>Mon, 14 Apr 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/headless/include-example-summary/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This is a similar markdown file in the &lt;code&gt;headless&lt;/code&gt; folder. It &lt;strong&gt;does&lt;/strong&gt; have a&#10;&lt;code&gt;params.includeSummary&lt;/code&gt; field in the frontmatter.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The &#10;&#10;&lt;a href="https://github.com/mrmxf/pihuw" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span style="color:red;"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:grey;"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:green;"&gt;H&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:grey;"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:blue;"&gt;W&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt; &lt;code&gt;include&lt;/code&gt; partial should not show this text because the&#10;frontmatter params override it. Try changing the name of the params parameter&#10;from &lt;code&gt;params.includeSummary&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;params.banana&lt;/code&gt; to sdee how the&#10;rendering changes.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Markdown files may include shortcodes.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Contact</title><link>https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/contact/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mrmxf.github.io/pihuw/contact/</guid><description>&lt;div class="card"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="card hi-1"&gt;&#10; &lt;h3&gt;Forms&lt;/h3&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;PicnicCSS is a static-site framework. Responding to a form needs a server to gather results.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;There are 2 easy solutions to make this work:&#10; &lt;ol&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;&amp;lt;iframe&amp;gt; Embed a free google form / Microsoft Form / Hubspot Form&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;Run a server in a container to handle responses&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;/ol&gt;&#10; &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;form&gt;&#10; &lt;h2&gt;Sample &lt;code&gt;picnic css&lt;/code&gt; contact form&lt;/h2&gt;&#10; &lt;div&gt;&#10; &lt;label&gt;First Name&lt;/label&gt;&#10; &lt;input type="text" name="first-name" placeholder="First Name"&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div&gt;&#10; &lt;label&gt;Last Name&lt;/label&gt;&#10; &lt;input type="text" name="last-name" placeholder="Last Name"&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div&gt;&#10; &lt;label class="checkable"&gt;&#10; &lt;input type="checkbox" tabindex="0"&gt;&#10; &lt;span&gt;I agree to the Terms and Conditions&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/label&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="button" type="submit"&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;&#10;&lt;/form&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>